# CAP practical-certification drills
#
# Recommended use:
# 1. Start the service with `npm run watch`.
# 2. Execute the requests manually.
# 3. Before looking at the source, predict the status code and response.
#
# VS Code/BAS REST Client variables:
@base = http://localhost:4004
@product = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@customer = aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa

### 1 — Inspect the OData service contract
GET {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/$metadata
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### 2 — Server-side projection, filter, sort, and paging
GET {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/Products?$select=ID,name,price,stock,stockStatus&$filter=active eq true&$orderby=price desc&$top=5
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### 3 — Localized business data in Indonesian
GET {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/Products({{product}})?$select=name,description
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer
Accept-Language: id

### 4 — Localized business data in German
GET {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/Products({{product}})?$select=name,description
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer
Accept-Language: de

### 5 — Read the current ETag for optimistic concurrency
# Copy the ETag response header and use it in request 6.
GET {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/Products({{product}})
Authorization: Basic editor editor

### 6 — Update only when the record has not changed
# Replace <paste-etag-here> with the ETag returned by request 5.
PATCH {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/Products({{product}})
Authorization: Basic editor editor
If-Match: <paste-etag-here>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stock": 12
}

### 7 — Observe authorization enforcement
# Expected: Viewer can read but cannot update.
PATCH {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/Products({{product}})
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stock": 99
}

### 8 — Deep create: header and owned items in one transaction
POST {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/Orders
Authorization: Basic editor editor
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_ID": "{{customer}}",
  "currency": "IDR",
  "note": "Certification drill",
  "items": [
    {
      "product_ID": "{{product}}",
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ]
}

### 9 — Expand the composition and association
GET {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/Orders?$expand=items($expand=product),customer&$orderby=createdAt desc&$top=3
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### 10 — Call a read-only function
GET {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/lowStock(threshold=15)
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### 11 — Call a state-changing unbound action
POST {{base}}/odata/v4/learning/restock
Authorization: Basic editor editor
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productID": "{{product}}",
  "quantity": 5
}

### 12 — Explore the draft-enabled service metadata
GET {{base}}/odata/v4/admin/$metadata
Authorization: Basic editor editor

### Exam simulation idea
# Delete or rename srv/admin-service.cds, then recreate a draft-enabled Orders
# service from memory in 15 minutes. Confirm your result through $metadata.
